# 🐧 3. Linux Administration

## 3.1 sudoers

The sudoers configuration controls which users or groups are allowed to use `sudo` and what elevated commands they may execute.

Main configuration file:

```text
/etc/sudoers
```

A safer way to edit the configuration is:

```bash
sudo visudo
```

### Interview Answer

> The sudoers configuration defines which users or groups can use sudo and what commands they are authorized to execute with elevated privileges.

