# 3.5 Bash Conditions

Bash can make decisions using conditional statements.

Example:

```bash
#!/bin/bash

if [ "$USER" = "root" ]; then
    echo "Root user"
else
    echo "Standard user"
fi
```

This demonstrates how scripts can make decisions based on conditions.

