# 🌐 4. Networking

## 4.1 Network Switch

A network switch connects devices within a LAN and forwards Ethernet frames based primarily on MAC addresses.

### Concept

```text
PC1 ──┐
PC2 ──┼── Switch
PC3 ──┘
```

### Interview Answer

> A network switch connects devices on a local network and forwards Ethernet frames based primarily on MAC addresses.

---

# 4.2 Access Port vs Trunk Port

## Access Port

Typically carries traffic for one VLAN.

```text
PC
 ↓
Access Port
 ↓
VLAN 10
```

## Trunk Port

Can carry traffic for multiple VLANs between network devices.

```text
Switch A
   ⇅
 Trunk
   ⇅
Switch B
```

### Important Correction

Do not confuse:

```text
VLAN ≠ VPN
```

### Memory

```text
Access
↓
One VLAN

Trunk
↓
Multiple VLANs
```

---

# 4.3 STP

STP stands for **Spanning Tree Protocol**.

It helps prevent Layer 2 switching loops when redundant network paths exist.

### Example

```text
Switch A
 ↘   ↖
  Switch B
```

Without loop prevention, redundant Layer 2 paths can cause network problems such as broadcast storms.

### Interview Answer

> STP helps prevent Layer 2 switching loops in networks with redundant links.

